04 4:49 Each man was registered as the LORD had commanded Moses; and at the command of the LORD given through Moses, each man was assigned responsibility for his task of serving or carrying.
04 5:1 The LORD said to Moses,
04 5:2 "Command the people of Israel to expel from the camp everyone with a dreaded skin disease or a bodily discharge and everyone who is unclean by contact with a corpse.
04 5:3 Send all these ritually unclean people out, so that they will not defile the camp, where I live among my people."
04 5:4 The Israelites obeyed and expelled them all from the camp.
04 5:5 The LORD gave Moses
04 5:6 the following instructions for the people of Israel. When any of you are unfaithful to the LORD and commit a wrong against someone,
04 5:7 you must confess your sin and make full repayment, plus an additional 20 percent, to the person you have wronged.
04 5:8 But if that person has died and has no near relative to whom payment can be made, it shall be given to the LORD for the priest. This payment is in addition to the ram used to perform the ritual of purification for the guilty person.
04 5:9 Also every special contribution which the Israelites offer to the LORD belongs to the priest to whom they present it.
04 5:10 Each priest shall keep the offerings presented to him.
04 5:11 The LORD commanded Moses
04 5:12 to give the Israelites the following instructions. It may happen that a man becomes suspicious that his wife is unfaithful to him and has defiled herself by having intercourse with another man.
04 5:13 But the husband may not be certain, for his wife may have kept it secret - there was no witness, and she was not caught in the act.
04 5:14 Or it may happen that a husband becomes suspicious of his wife, even though she has not been unfaithful.
04 5:15 In either case the man shall take his wife to the priest. He shall also take the required offering of two pounds of barley flour, but he shall not pour any olive oil on it or put any incense on it, because it is an offering from a suspicious husband, made to bring the truth to light.
04 5:16 The priest shall bring the woman forward and have her stand in front of the altar.
04 5:17 He shall pour some holy water into a clay bowl and take some of the earth that is on the floor of the Tent of the LORD's presence and put it in the water to make it bitter.
04 5:18 Then he shall loosen the woman's hair and put the offering of flour in her hands. In his hands the priest shall hold the bowl containing the bitter water that brings a curse.
04 5:19 Then the priest shall make the woman agree to this oath spoken by the priest： "If you have not committed adultery, you will not be harmed by the curse that this water brings.
04 5:20 But if you have committed adultery,
04 5:21 may the LORD make your name a curse among your people. May he cause your genital organs to shrink and your stomach to swell up.
04 5:22 May this water enter your stomach and cause it to swell up and your genital organs to shrink." The woman shall respond, "I agree; may the LORD do so."
04 5:23 Then the priest shall write this curse down and wash the writing off into the bowl of bitter water.
04 5:24 Before he makes the woman drink the water, which may then cause her bitter pain,
04 5:25 the priest shall take the offering of flour out of the woman's hands, hold it out in dedication to the LORD, and present it on the altar.
04 5:26 Then he shall take a handful of it as a token offering and burn it on the altar. Finally, he shall make the woman drink the water.
04 5:27 If she has committed adultery, the water will cause bitter pain; her stomach will swell up and her genital organs will shrink. Her name will become a curse among her people.
04 5:28 But if she is innocent, she will not be harmed and will be able to bear children.
04 5:29 This is the law in cases where a man is jealous and becomes suspicious that his wife has committed adultery.
04 5:30 The woman shall be made to stand in front of the altar, and the priest shall perform this ritual.
04 5:31 The husband shall be free of guilt, but the woman, if guilty, must suffer the consequences.
04 6:1 The LORD commanded Moses
04 6:2 to give the following instructions to the people of Israel. Any of you, male or female, who make a special vow to become a nazirite and dedicate yourself to the LORD
04 6:3 shall abstain from wine and beer. You shall not drink any kind of drink made from grapes or eat any grapes or raisins.
04 6:4 As long as you are a nazirite, you shall not eat anything that comes from a grapevine, not even the seeds or skins of grapes.
04 6:5 As long as you are under the nazirite vow, you must not cut your hair or shave. You are bound by the vow for the full time that you are dedicated to the LORD, and you shall let your hair grow.
04 6:6 Your hair is the sign of your dedication to God,
04 6:7 and so you must not defile yourself by going near a corpse, not even that of your father, mother, brother, or sister.
04 6:8 As long as you are a nazirite, you are consecrated to the LORD.
04 6:9 If your consecrated hair is defiled because you are right beside someone who suddenly dies, you must wait seven days and then shave your head; and so you become ritually clean.
04 6:10 On the eighth day you shall bring two doves or two pigeons to the priest at the entrance of the Tent of the LORD's presence.
04 6:11 The priest shall offer one as a sin offering and the other as a burnt offering, to perform the ritual of purification for you because of your contact with a corpse. On the same day you shall reconsecrate your hair
04 6:12 and rededicate to the LORD your time as a nazirite. The previous period of time doesn't count, because your consecrated hair was defiled. As a repayment offering you shall bring a one-year-old lamb.
04 6:13 When you complete your nazirite vow, you shall perform this ritual. You shall go to the entrance of the Tent
04 6:14 and present to the LORD three animals without any defects： a one-year-old male lamb for a burnt offering, a one-year-old ewe lamb for a sin offering, and a ram for a fellowship offering.
04 6:15 You shall also offer a basket of bread made without yeast： thick loaves made of flour mixed with olive oil and thin cakes brushed with olive oil, and in addition the required offerings of grain and wine.
04 6:16 The priest shall present all these to the LORD and offer the sin offering and the burnt offering.
04 6:17 He shall sacrifice the ram to the LORD as a fellowship offering, and offer it with the basket of bread; he shall also present the offerings of grain and wine.
04 6:18 At the entrance of the Tent you nazirites shall shave off your hair and put it on the fire on which the fellowship offering is being burned.
04 6:19 Then, when the shoulder of the ram is boiled, the priest shall take it and put it, together with one thick loaf of bread and one thin cake from the basket, into the hands of the nazirite.
04 6:20 Next, the priest shall present them as a special gift to the LORD; they are a sacred offering for the priest, in addition to the breast and the leg of the ram which by law belong to the priest. After that, the nazirite may drink wine.
04 6:21 These are the regulations for you nazirites; but if you promise an offering beyond what your vow requires you to give, you must fulfill exactly the promise you made.
04 6:22 The LORD commanded Moses
04 6:23 to tell Aaron and his sons to use the following words in blessing the people of Israel：
04 6:24 May the LORD bless you and take care of you;
04 6:25 May the LORD be kind and gracious to you;
04 6:26 May the LORD look on you with favor and give you peace.
04 6:27 And the LORD said, "If they pronounce my name as a blessing upon the people of Israel, I will bless them."
04 7:1 On the day Moses finished setting up the Tent of the LORD's presence, he anointed and dedicated the Tent and all its equipment, and the altar and all its equipment.
04 7:2 Then the clan chiefs who were leaders in the tribes of Israel, the same men who were in charge of the census,
04 7:3 brought their offerings to the LORD： six wagons and twelve oxen, a wagon for every two leaders and an ox for each leader. After they had presented them,
04 7:4 the LORD said to Moses,
04 7:5 "Accept these gifts for use in the work to be done for the Tent; give them to the Levites according to the work they have to do."
04 7:6 So Moses gave the wagons and the oxen to the Levites.
04 7:7 He gave two wagons and four oxen to the Gershonites,
04 7:8 and four wagons and eight oxen to the Merarites. All their work was to be done under the direction of Ithamar son of Aaron.
04 7:9 But Moses gave no wagons or oxen to the Kohathites, because the sacred objects they took care of had to be carried on their shoulders.
04 7:10 The leaders also brought offerings to celebrate the dedication of the altar. When they were ready to present their gifts at the altar,
04 7:11 the LORD said to Moses, "Tell them that each day for a period of twelve days one of the leaders is to present his gifts for the dedication of the altar."
04 7:12 They presented their offerings in the following order： [Day： Tribe： Leader]
04 7:13 1st： Judah： Nahshon son of Amminadab,
04 7:14 2nd： Issachar： Nethanel son of Zuar,
04 7:15 3rd： Zebulun： Eliab son of Helon,
04 7:16 4th： Reuben： Elizur son of Shedeur,
04 7:17 5th： Simeon： Shelumiel son of Zurishaddai,
04 7:18 6th： Gad： Eliasaph son of Deuel,
04 7:19 7th： Ephraim： Elishama son of Ammihud,
04 7:20 8th： Manasseh： Gamaliel son of Pedahzur,
04 7:21 9th： Benjamin： Abidan son of Gideoni,
04 7:22 10th： Dan： Ahiezer son of Ammishaddai,
04 7:23 11th： Asher： Pagiel son of Ochran,
04 7:24 12th： Naphtali： Ahira son of Enan.
04 7:25 The offerings each one brought were identical：
04 7:26 one silver bowl weighing 50 ounces
04 7:27 and one silver basin weighing 30 ounces,
04 7:28 by the official standard,
04 7:29 both of them full of flour mixed with oil for the grain offering;
04 7:30 one gold dish weighing 4 ounces,
04 7:31 full of incense;
04 7:32 one young bull,
04 7:33 one ram,
04 7:34 and a one-year-old lamb,
04 7:35 for the burnt offering;
04 7:36 one goat for the sin offering;
04 7:37 and two bulls,
04 7:38 five rams,
04 7:39 five goats,
04 7:40 and five one-year-old lambs,
04 7:41 for the fellowship offering.
